completionSummary:
CQ-R11a: guest-supervisor.py gains a root-only 'check' mode (main(['check']) -> check_job).

Intake: read_check reads one frame (read_frame, extracted from read_job; read_job is unchanged) and checks:
- exact keys {kind:'check', version, id, command, protected};
- version is an int and equals 1;
- id matches the daemon regex;
- command is non-blank by JS trim, has no C0/C1/U+2028/U+2029 characters, and is at most 1000 UTF-16 units;
- protected == [].

Exit codes: a bad frame gives 65, EOF 74, no moe-check account or session home 71, a missing workspace 66, non-root 77, bad argv 64. None writes a frame or starts a job.

Re-own: reown() walks the workspace through directory fds. It lstats each entry and refuses links, FIFOs and other specials, a hard-linked file, a path over MAX_PATH_BYTES, and a lstat/open (dev, ino, type) mismatch. Every chown is an fchown.

Spawn: relay(['/bin/sh','-c',command]) with no agent socket and:
- user/group moe-check with no extra groups;
- umask 077;
- cwd = the workspace;
- env exactly PATH, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, LANG and MOE_CHECK_ID;
- CQ-R11d's rlimits, soft = hard;
- a private netns.

GUARD applies the rlimits and, when netns is set, unshares the network and brings lo up after the NNP prctl. The agent job path is unchanged.

Tests (local-runner-check.test.mjs):
- K1: about 50 refusal rows;
- K2: the recorder contract and drift against CHECK_BOUNDARIES;
- K3: a real Linux job read from /proc (env, cwd, Umask, NoNewPrivs, limits);
- K4: the fd walk (symlink, hard link, FIFO, swap, depth, fchown failure).

The bridge test is unchanged. Mutation check: 49/50 killed; the survivor (the S_IFMT re-check) is equivalent outside inode reuse. The netns branch was verified ad hoc under unshare -r and is not a suite row; CQ-R13 certifies it.

